+## Measured semantics
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+- `beforeSession` is inside the `try` block, so a throw there reaches the `catch`/`finally` blocks, firing both `onError` and `afterSession`; `afterSession` runs by design for a `beforeSession` that never completed, and a deployer can assume no tools were run and the turn was aborted before provider interaction — but a hook cannot tell "never allocated" from "allocated and finished" from the session alone, so one that allocates in `beforeSession` and must not double-release marks the allocation itself ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
 
-- `beforeSession` is awaited before the `try` block opens ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L91](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L91)), so a throw there escapes before the `catch`/`finally` exist and skips both `onError` and `afterSession`.
-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+## Recorded flaws — out of scope
+
+Three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` were recorded by re-cinq/HALEngine#83 so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour; the first of the three was a flaw owned by no issue, and re-cinq/HALEngine#94 owns its repair now — its guarantee is the cited statement above. The remaining two are still recorded flaws, each owned by no issue in this epic.
+
